From: Anaphygon <349679039+Anaphygon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:43:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: a port can stand in for game functions and mix its own
 sound

UN5's movies are to be decoded on the host (un5-nx ports/un5/movie.cpp):
the game's player stays, and only its leaves that touch the IPU, the CD
stream and the SPU2 are replaced. That needs:

- eerecomp --hooks <file>: the listed functions ask ps2::hook() at their
  entry, and a stand-in registered with ps2::register_hook() may do the
  work and return (or tail-call elsewhere). The declarations are in
  ps2/hook.hpp, which only the units holding a hooked entry include, so a
  new hook rebuilds those alone.
- ps2::set_audio_mix(): a port's sound added to the SPU2's output before
  the sink and the recording take it.
- disc::read under a mutex: the movie decoder reads the image from its own
  thread, and the reader seeks a shared handle.
- CMake builds native_*.c as well, for a port's C sources (libmpeg2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
